# ThreatForge Output — SIGNATURES
# CVE:       CVE-2026-16812
# Product:   velocloud_orchestrator
# Tags:      [KEV] [RCE] [RCE-KEV] [CRIT] [NEW]
# Score:     155
# Tier:      CRITICAL — ACT NOW
# Generated: 2026-07-30T02:02:24.251077Z
# Status:    OK
# ---

# Confidence: No public PoC known — pattern inferred from the CVE/advisory
# description only. The CISA KEV entry [2] and vendor advisory [5] describe
# this as a broken access control / OS command injection vulnerability in
# VeloCloud Orchestrator On-Prem that allows remote access to privileged
# internal functionality over the network (AV:N/PR:N/UI:N, CVSS 10.0 [1]).
# The rule targets HTTP requests to path prefixes associated with internal/
# privileged VCO API endpoints that would not be legitimately reachable from
# external sources. No specific endpoint URI was disclosed in available
# sources; "/portal/rest/v1/system/admin" and "/vco/api/v1/system" are
# representative internal API path prefixes inferred from general VeloCloud
# Orchestrator architecture — these MUST be validated against your VCO
# deployment before deployment. An anomalous HTTP method (POST) from an
# external source targeting these paths is the observable behaviour modelled.
# No packet-capture (PCAP) data source is available to this pipeline —
# this pattern is NOT verified against captured exploit traffic.
# DRAFT FOR ANALYST REVIEW — do not deploy without endpoint validation
# against your VeloCloud Orchestrator instance and review of vendor
# advisory [5] for confirmed affected URI paths.

alert http $EXTERNAL_NET any -> $HOME_NET any (
  msg:"THREATFORGE CVE-2026-16812 VeloCloud Orchestrator privileged internal API access attempt";
  flow:established,to_server;
  http.method; content:"POST";
  http.uri; content:"/portal/rest/"; nocase;
  pcre:"/\/portal\/rest\/(v[0-9]+\/)?(system|admin|diagnostics|configuration|internalApi)/i";
  threshold:type both, track by_src, count 3, seconds 10;
  reference:cve,2026-16812;
  metadata:mitre_technique_id T1190, is_kev true, status experimental;
  classtype:attempted-admin;
  sid:9000044; rev:1; )

